#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151827 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24db328-4a49-5002-b0af-635d0c0d89b9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Step Function"}] :question/id #uuid "da59a348-2112-505c-824d-9e8df8409127" :question/math-academy-id "e-21591" :question/problem "Evaluate $f(t) = 9u(t-9)$ at $t=9,$ where $u$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(t)$ at $t=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(9) & =9u(9-9) \\\\  & =9u(0) \\\\  & =9\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(9)=9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151828 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f7a33f8-b0f6-5265-9d3e-c1ca34c07161" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Transformed Step Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "718a239f-9b43-5b4d-b638-b0f64be196fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-21592" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/fe9901de89c17bccdaa8c0f95440a079e6537dc42fe858fd836d89eb62f29ca7.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/666fe470145e36e88a33d0719268c25226606d4de10e57f1a8e97ccfa4d34eaa.png)\n\nNotice that to transform $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we shift $y=u(t)$ by $2$ units to the left, giving $y=u(t+2).$\n\n- Then, we scale $y=u(t+2)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=3u(t+2).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=3u(t+2).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151829 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "253b1011-a313-5004-8cbe-61133586e6b1" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Reflected Step Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "c13d67e8-db9e-5d02-a501-98f8987169fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21594" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/74bc7efebfaa6a798b848d9f0bbc400bc84a727a933fef32069fec6a87e6ed6b.png)\n\nThe graph of $y = f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y = u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/666fe470145e36e88a33d0719268c25226606d4de10e57f1a8e97ccfa4d34eaa.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y = u(t)$ to the given function $y = f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we reflect $y = u(t)$ in the $y$-axis, which gives $y = u(-t).$\n\n- Next, we shift by one unit to the left, giving $y = u(-(t+1)) = u(-1 - t).$\n\n- Finally, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y = 2u(-1 - t).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t) = 2u(-1 - t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f7a33f8-b0f6-5265-9d3e-c1ca34c07161" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Transformed Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ffbb67b0-cdb6-5a80-a77c-d557c3a1dad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(t-1)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305160} {:answer/id #uuid "9897b502-a26a-5ea2-b545-f024841ec582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305161} {:answer/id #uuid "5da9e907-aa4f-5f60-8463-5d39b6a89900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305162} {:answer/id #uuid "8af50beb-c843-54f4-8247-547147ee4e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(t+1)+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305163} {:answer/id #uuid "184e7c5f-3d47-5706-9076-adb0c3a1e6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5da9e907-aa4f-5f60-8463-5d39b6a89900" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305162} :answer-field/id #uuid "078e107b-7b29-5a1f-9685-66391c09a6b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "667d57dc-7eb9-57bc-b685-cfc00950512e" :question/math-academy-id "q-331185" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/6f80319af7f362c2a902853687670a9dab8e88778521147942dfb9a0d9872b75.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t),$ where $u$ denotes the unit step function?" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/4f7a1a32f5c639ec0a9433fc6d330e5ea9f8ed6fa1602441b54c9158bb69f63e.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we shift $y=u(t)$ by one unit to the right, giving $y=u(t-1).$\n\n- Then, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=2u(t-1).$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=2u(t-1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24db328-4a49-5002-b0af-635d0c0d89b9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Step Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a36951a-25b4-5723-87b3-6311335079ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a36951a-25b4-5723-87b3-6311335079ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305167} :answer-field/id #uuid "230806bd-296f-5194-bc9a-25180b584253" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "00d2d6b2-1fae-52c2-a8c5-493a320ab1cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-331230" :question/problem "Evaluate $f(t)=7u(t-1)$ at $t=-4,$ where $u$ is the unit step function.\n\n$f(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nu(t)={\\begin{aligned}1,\\,t\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(t)$ at $t=-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =7u(-4-1) \\\\  & =7u(-5) \\\\  & =7\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(-4)=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24db328-4a49-5002-b0af-635d0c0d89b9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Step Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "270993ba-681b-51b8-8b61-73b2be5682ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "270993ba-681b-51b8-8b61-73b2be5682ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305170} :answer-field/