\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\,t<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14037461/assets/a1748c6e23d99ad6ef43d5aceedcadb7a12fcdbef5064f93202d2fe5ca3d98d7.png)\n\nNotice that to transform $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t),$ we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we reflect $y=u(t)$ in the $y$-axis, which gives $y=u(-t).$\n\n- Next, we shift by one unit to the left, giving $y=u(-(t+1))=u(-1-t).$\n\n- There is no vertical scaling or offset.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $f(t)=u(-1-t).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152481 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "253b1011-a313-5004-8cbe-61133586e6b1" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Reflected Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a1dc98f-e340-5d3c-8174-4c99cde26caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(-t) + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149727} {:answer/id #uuid "2508f5f8-2132-52e1-8979-e0731b7b59c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u(-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149728} {:answer/id #uuid "25383acd-d6da-511e-8d23-4ee57a11beeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149729} {:answer/id #uuid "72da048a-98e4-58a0-a4b0-8a76a7e6020e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149730} {:answer/id #uuid "7e69f8f0-f498-5dfb-8c06-91e097d169d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25383acd-d6da-511e-8d23-4ee57a11beeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(-t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149729} :answer-field/id #uuid "166158bb-6065-51bd-a90a-ee48f21cdc91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149726}] :